Fideslang taxonomy
------------------
Files:   vendor/taxonomy/data_categories.json
         vendor/taxonomy/data_subjects.json
         vendor/taxonomy/data_uses.json
Source:  https://github.com/ethyca/fideslang
         src/fideslang/default_taxonomy/{data_categories,data_uses,data_subjects}.py
Author:  © Ethyca, Inc.
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This is a MODIFIED redistribution: the upstream Python definitions were reformatted to JSON and
reduced to the `fides_key`, `name` and `description` fields. No other change was made to the
meaning of any entry. The files are verbatim copies of the snapshot maintained in
noru-tech/noru-grc-engineering (contract/lib/taxonomy/), taxonomy directory last modified at
upstream commit 21eb1746904d (2024-11-04), latest published release at snapshot time 3.1.3.
Provenance and the refresh recipe are in vendor/SOURCE.md.

vendor/taxonomy/special_categories.json selects which Fideslang keys GDPR Articles 9 and 10
treat as special. The keys are Ethyca's under CC BY 4.0; the selection is Noru's own and is
MIT-licensed with the rest of the code.

Field-name classification table
-------------------------------
File:    vendor/classification/classification.json
Source:  noru-tech/noru-grc-engineering, plugins/privacy-datamap/references/classification.json
Author:  Noru
License: MIT

The table maps field names to Fideslang data category keys (CC BY 4.0, above). It is reused
verbatim so that privacy-datamap (which maps what a repository stores) and privacy-flow (which
maps where it sends it) classify a field name the same way.

This repository's own code is MIT-licensed. The vendored taxonomy data remains CC BY 4.0.
